// =====================================================================
// P3 - OneLake availability on the raw telemetry table.
// Makes the KQL table readable as a Delta table from OneLake, so a
// Fabric notebook (or Spark, or AML) can read it without exporting.
// =====================================================================

// Syntax notes (verified against Microsoft Learn, do not "fix" this):
//   - dataformat MUST be "parquet". Delta is the resulting layout, not an
//     accepted parameter value. "dataformat=delta" returns a bare BadRequest.
//   - .alter-merge keeps the auto-populated ConnectionStrings property that
//     Fabric maintains itself; a plain .alter would overwrite the whole policy.
//   - TargetLatencyInMinutes is NOT cosmetic here. The default write delay is
//     "up to 3 hours, or until 200-256 MB files are created". With a trickle of
//     sensor data that means the Delta table stays EMPTY for the whole demo.
//     5 minutes is the documented minimum (allowed range: 5 min - 3 h).
//     Trade-off accepted: more small parquet files, irrelevant at this volume.

.alter-merge table telemetry policy mirroring dataformat=parquet with (IsEnabled=true, TargetLatencyInMinutes=5)

// Verify - Policy must no longer be null, and must show "IsEnabled": true.
// The returned ConnectionStrings field is authoritative: it contains the real
// OneLake path of the mirrored table, expressed with GUIDs:
//   https://westus3-api.onelake.fabric.microsoft.com/{workspaceId}/{kqlDatabaseId}/Tables/telemetry/
// i.e. for this demo, read it from Spark as:
//   abfss://<FABRIC_WORKSPACE_ID>@onelake.dfs.fabric.microsoft.com/<KQL_DATABASE_ID>/Tables/telemetry
// Note it is the KQL DATABASE id in the path, not the Eventhouse id.
.show table telemetry policy mirroring

// NOT SUPPORTED on this Eventhouse (returns a permanent SyntaxException):
//   .show table telemetry mirroring operations
// Monitor freshness from the portal instead: Explorer > table > More menu >
// View files, and check the _delta_log folder timestamps.
//
// "Backfill": false in the policy means only data ingested AFTER enabling is
// guaranteed to be mirrored. Always verify the row count from the notebook
// before training rather than assuming history came along.
//
// Mirroring is asynchronous: allow at least one TargetLatencyInMinutes window
// after enabling before the first Delta files appear.
